<p>When this photo appeared in the <em>Loveland</em> [Colo.] <em>Reporter</em> in 1895, farmer Joseph B. Swan was besieged with requests for pieces and seeds of his giant potato &#8212; the story implied that it was 2 feet 5 inches long and weighed more than 86 pounds.</p>
<p>Editor W.L. Thorndyke was forced to admit the spud had been carved out of wood &#8212; they&#8217;d arranged the hoax to promote a local street fair.</p>
